local clock reaches the daily release time\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A dedicated holder releases today's space after the configured daily release time\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response indicates that the space is available immediately\",\n     \"when\": \"the release request completes\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a scheduled release reaches the daily release time or a same-day release occurs, the Folio3 parking web app shall make the space claimable at the daily release time for scheduled releases and same-day releases before that time, and immediately for same-day releases after that time.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"Q-2\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"One space is available and two eligible employees submit claims concurrently\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"exactly one response confirms a claim, the other response rejects it, and the returned available-space count is zero\",\n     \"when\": \"the claim requests are processed\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An eligible employee opens the parking availability view\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.2\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the current available-space count\",\n     \"when\": \"spaces are available\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An employee with dedicated parking submits a temporary-space claim\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response rejects the claim\",\n     \"when\": \"the claim request is processed\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall provide available-space counts and allocate each available space to the first eligible non-dedicated employee whose claim is accepted, allowing each space to be claimed only once.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An employee has multiple registered vehicles and an available space exists\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the returned allocation record contains the selected plate as the only authorized plate and the assigned floor has the greatest remaining capacity, subject to the configured consistent tie-break\",\n     \"when\": \"the employee claims the space using one selected vehicle\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An employee has a successful temporary claim\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.2\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays the assigned parking floor\",\n     \"when\": \"the employee views the allocation\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An employee submits a temporary claim without selecting a registered vehicle\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response rejects the claim and the response field identifies vehicle selection as required\",\n     \"when\": \"the claim is processed\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall require an employee claiming temporary parking to select one registered vehicle, authorize only that vehicle's plate for the allocation, and assign a floor with the most remaining capacity using a consistent tie-break when floors have equal remaining capacity.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-3\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"At least one parking space becomes available and eligible non-dedicated employees have email addresses\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the outbound email-service call contains the eligible recipients and a fixed-template message\",\n     \"when\": \"the availability notification is processed\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When one or more parking spaces become available, the Folio3 parking web app shall send an email notification using a fixed template to eligible employees without dedicated parking.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"ASM-1\",\n    \"ASM-14\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An employee has an active temporary parking claim\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response rejects the request and the returned claim record remains active\",\n     \"when\": \"the employee submits a cancellation request\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall reject employee cancellation of a temporary parking claim in Phase 1.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"ASM-15\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n   \"ears\": \"When the existing entrance LPR camera reports a car plate detection, the Folio3 parking web app shall verify the plate against an active temporary allocation for the office-local date, request green-indicator activation only for valid authorization, and record the attempt's date, time, plate, verification result, and entry status.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"ASM-2\",\n    \"ASM-12\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A detected car plate has a valid temporary allocation for the office-local date\",\n     \"when\": \"the entrance verification interface processes the detection\",\n     \"then\": \"the verification row records the date, time, plate, authorized verification result, and entry status, the outbound indicator call requests green activation, and the response reports an authorized result\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.2\",\n     \"given\": \"A detected car plate has no valid temporary allocation for the office-local date\",\n     \"when\": \"the entrance verification interface processes the detection\",\n     \"then\": \"the verification row records the date, time, plate, unauthorized verification result, and entry status, the outbound indicator call does not request green activation, and the response reports an unauthorized result\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-15.3\",\n     \"given\": \"The LPR camera reports a pedestrian, motorcycle, or other non-car object\",\n     \"when\": \"the detection is processed\",\n     \"then\": \"the response contains no parking authorization result and no green-activation call is sent\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall record permanent-sticker vehicle plate detections for utilization, bypass temporary authorization and entry blocking for those vehicles, and, when a permanent holder enters a released space allocated temporarily, cancel that temporary allocation so subsequent verification denies the temporary claimant authorization for that space.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"Q-6\",\n    \"Q-8\",\n    \"Q-12\",\n    \"ASM-11\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A permanent-sticker vehicle detection is received, including when its dedicated holder released the space and another employee claimed it\",\n     \"when\": \"the detection is processed\",\n     \"then\": \"a detection row is recorded and no temporary-authorization decision or entry-blocking call is made for that vehicle\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.2\",\n     \"given\": \"A security guard checks an entrance result\",\n     \"when\": \"the guard-facing surface is accessed\",\n     \"then\": \"the screen displays only the indicator result and exposes no parking records or product screen\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.3\",\n     \"given\": \"A permanent-sticker holder is detected entering a released space with an active temporary allocation\",\n     \"when\": \"the permanent holder's detection is processed\",\n     \"then\": \"the permanent-vehicle detection row is recorded and the temporary allocation row has a canceled status\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-16.4\",\n     \"given\": \"A permanent-sticker holder's detected entry has canceled the temporary allocation for the space\",\n     \"when\": \"the temporary claimant's plate is processed by the entrance verification interface\",\n     \"then\": \"the response reports an unauthorized result and the outbound indicator call does not request green activation\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n   \"ears\": \"If the camera, plate recognition, network, or indicator fails or a plate cannot be read during an entrance check, then the Folio3 parking web app shall record an unsuccessful verification, keep green authorization off, and deny entry until service is restored without offering a manual-verification path.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"ASM-3\",\n    \"ASM-13\",\n    \"Q-10\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.1\",\n     \"given\": \"An entrance check encounters a camera, recognition, network, or indicator failure, or an unreadable plate\",\n     \"when\": \"the verification interface processes the failure\",\n     \"then\": \"the response reports an unsuccessful result with an entry-status field of Denied, the verification row records the failure, no green-activation call is issued, and no manual-verification path is offered\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-17.2\",\n     \"given\": \"Entrance service has been restored and a detected plate has a valid temporary allocation for the office-local date\",\n     \"when\": \"the verification interface processes the detection\",\n     \"then\": \"the response reports an authorized result and the outbound indicator call requests green activation\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A dedicated holder did not release a working-day space and no registered vehicle entry exists for that date\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.1\",\n     \"level\": \"job\",\n     \"then\": \"a utilization row records Unused Dedicated Parking with the employee, vehicle, and date fields\",\n     \"when\": \"the utilization evaluation runs\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An employee claimed temporary parking and the selected vehicle has no entry detection on the claim date\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.2\",\n     \"level\": \"job\",\n     \"then\": \"a utilization row records Unused Temporary Parking with the employee, vehicle, and date fields\",\n     \"when\": \"the utilization evaluation runs\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A permanent-sticker vehicle enters the facility\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the detection row is available to the utilization evaluation\",\n     \"when\": \"its entry detection is processed for utilization\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall record an Unused Dedicated Parking event for each working day when a dedicated holder did not release the space and no registered vehicle entry was detected, and an Unused Temporary Parking event when a claimant's selected vehicle was not detected entering on the claim date.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"Q-7\",\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Utilization history exists for the reporting week\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.1\",\n     \"level\": \"job\",\n     \"then\": \"the generated report file contains the dedicated-unused and temporary-unused employee lists, daily and weekly statistics, released-space count, temporary-claim count, and an overall utilization-percentage field\",\n     \"when\": \"the Monday-morning report job runs\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall generate a weekly utilization report every Monday morning in the office timezone containing dedicated employees who neither released nor used their parking, temporary claimants who did not use their parking, daily and weekly utilization statistics, total released spaces, total temporary claims, and an overall utilization percentage.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-19\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"ASM-4\",\n    \"ASM-17\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A weekly report is generated and designated stakeholder email addresses are configured\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.1\",\n     \"level\": \"job\",\n     \"then\": \"the outbound email-service call contains the stakeholder recipients and the generated report\",\n     \"when\": \"the report email job runs\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An authenticated parking administrator changes the designated stakeholder recipient list\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the returned recipient list contains the updated addresses\",\n     \"when\": \"the list is read for the next report\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An authenticated employee who is not a parking administrator submits a stakeholder recipient-list update\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"the response status is non-success and the returned recipient list remains unchanged\",\n     \"when\": \"the update request is processed\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall email each weekly utilization report to the designated stakeholders using the configured stakeholder recipient list and permit only authenticated parking administrators to update that list.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-20\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"ASM-18\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A utilization evaluation identifies unused dedicated or temporary parking\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-21.1\",\n     \"level\": \"job\",\n     \"then\": \"no warning, suspension, or penalty row, event, email, or outbound enforcement call is created\",\n     \"when\": \"the evaluation and report jobs run\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall not create automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties based on parking utilization in Phase 1.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-21\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-6\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A test retention policy is configured for release, claim, LPR verification, and utilization history\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-22.1\",\n     \"level\": \"job\",\n     \"then\": \"the row list retains in-period records and removes or archives expired records according to the policy\",\n     \"when\": \"the retention job runs across records both within and beyond the configured retention period\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall retain release, claim, LPR verification, and utilization history according to Folio3's existing records-retention policy.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-22\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"I-6\",\n    \"Q-5\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n   \"metric\": \"0 horizontal overflow at 320, 768, and 1440 CSS-pixel viewport widths; touch targets are at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels.\",\n   \"text\": \"The product is one responsive web app with layouts for phone, tablet, and desktop; all pages avoid horizontal overflow at representative widths and narrow layouts use touch-sized controls.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"outOfScope\": [\n  \"Native iOS or Android applications, app-store distribution, native push notifications, background location, and native home-screen behavior; the product is a responsive web app, with email used for availability notifications (ASM-1, ASM-14).\",\n  \"SMS notifications (ASM-1, ASM-14).\",\n  \"Custom report builder (ASM-4, ASM-17).\",\n  \"Offline parking flows (ASM-8).\"\n ],\n \"assumptions\": [\n  \"ASM-1 and ASM-14: availability notices use fixed-template email only; SMS and push notifications are excluded.\",\n  \"ASM-2 and ASM-12: integration uses the existing LPR camera and indicator through their supported interfaces; the vendor and interface remain to be identified.\",\n  \"ASM-3 and ASM-13: entrance verification fails closed; entry is denied until service is restored, with no manual-verification path.\",\n  \"ASM-5: English-only, left-to-right content.\",\n  \"ASM-6: support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\",\n  \"ASM-7: WCAG 2.1 AA applies to main flows.\",\n  \"ASM-8: parking flows are online-only.\",\n  \"ASM-9: light mode only.\",\n  \"ASM-10: capacity assumption is up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year; no peak concurrent-claim number is established.\",\n  \"ASM-11: record permanent-sticker plate detections for utilization, without using them to authorize or block entry.\",\n  \"ASM-15: employees cannot cancel temporary claims in Phase 1.\",\n  \"ASM-16: a self-registered plate becomes active immediately.\",\n  \"ASM-18: designated report recipients are represented by a configured recipient list; the assumption text does not specify a recipient-management mechanism.\",\n  \"The utilization-percentage formula is not established by ASM-4 or ASM-17; the report includes a percentage field, but its calculation needs confirmation.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<failures>\nYour previous attempt was rejected for these reasons. Fix them:\n- [spec-lint L3 ears] REQ-15 needs exactly one \"shall\"\n</failures>\n\nReview the spec."}